IMPORT daydate

-- Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) -- the date arithmetic the baseline needs, kept in one
-- small module so that the daydate library is imported once. Every other module of this encoding imports this one, not
-- daydate.

§ `Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (WA) -- dates`

-- A date written day, month, year (for the cases file, which does not import daydate).
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` d m y MEANS Date d m y

-- Schedule 7 cl 31(2): "If a period beginning on a given day, act or event is provided or allowed for a purpose by this
-- Law, the period is to be calculated by excluding the day, or the day of the act or event, and -- ... (b) in any other
-- case -- by including the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled." So "within 60 days after receipt" ends on the
-- 60th day after the day of receipt.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, start IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the nth day after` n start MEANS Date (Day start PLUS n)

-- Schedule 7 cl 31(3): "If the last day of a period provided or allowed by this Law for doing anything is not a business
-- day in the place in which the thing is to be or may be done, the thing may be done on the next business day in the
-- place." cl 12(1): a business day is a day that is not "(a) a Saturday or Sunday; or (b) a public holiday, special
-- holiday or bank holiday in the place". Only (a) is worked out here: public holidays depend on the place, which the
-- Law does not fix for a National Board (see NOTES.md), so they are not encoded.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next weekday from` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Weekday of` d EQUALS Saturday THEN Date (Day d PLUS 2)
        IF `Weekday of` d EQUALS Sunday   THEN Date (Day d PLUS 1)
        OTHERWISE d

-- The last day of a period of n days after start, moved past a Saturday or Sunday.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, start IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` n `days after` start MEANS `the next weekday from` (`the nth day after` n start)

-- s 161(3): "at not less than 3 monthly intervals". Three months from a day fall on the same day number three months on;
-- where that month is shorter, on its last day (daydate's `add months` clamps). Moved past a Saturday or Sunday by
-- Schedule 7 cl 31(3).
GIVEN start IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of 3 months after` start MEANS `the next weekday from` (`add months` start 3)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls on or before` b IF Day a AT MOST Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls before` b IF Day a LESS THAN Day b

-- The number of days from a to b (for the regulative rules, whose WITHIN counts days from the start of the period).
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` a `to` b MEANS Day b MINUS Day a

-- The day sections 237A and 237B commenced: the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law and Other Legislation
-- Amendment Act 2025 (Qld) s 22 inserted them, and Part 3 of that Act (other than ss 16-21 and 23) commenced on
-- 1 December 2025 (compilation table, citing Qld SL 2025/139).
`the day sections 237A and 237B commenced` MEANS Date 1 12 2025
